{"data": {"id": "10.5281/zenodo.24408074", "type": "dois", "attributes": {"doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24408074", "prefix": "10.5281", "suffix": "zenodo.24408074", "identifiers": [], "alternateIdentifiers": [], "creators": [{"name": "Min-Gi, Kim", "nameType": "Personal", "givenName": "Kim", "familyName": "Min-Gi", "affiliation": ["Independent Researcher, OrganOS"], "nameIdentifiers": []}], "titles": [{"title": "Sensor Confirmation Timing and False Alarms in Oil Well Anomaly Detection: An Exploratory Study Using Petrobras 3W Field Records"}], "publisher": "Zenodo", "container": {}, "publicationYear": 2026, "subjects": [{"subject": "Oil Well Anomaly Detection"}, {"subject": "Sensor Time Series"}, {"subject": "Temporal Confirmation"}, {"subject": "False Alarms"}, {"subject": "Industrial Monitoring"}, {"subject": "Petrobras 3W"}, {"subject": "Reproducible Research"}, {"subject": "OrganOS"}], "contributors": [], "dates": [{"date": "2026-11-20", "dateType": "Issued"}], "language": "en", "types": {"ris": "GEN", "bibtex": "misc", "citeproc": "article", "schemaOrg": "CreativeWork", "resourceType": "", "resourceTypeGeneral": "Preprint"}, "relatedIdentifiers": [{"relationType": "Cites", "relatedIdentifier": "10.6084/m9.figshare.29205836.v1", "resourceTypeGeneral": "Dataset", "relatedIdentifierType": "DOI"}, {"relationType": "Cites", "relatedIdentifier": "10.1038/s41597-026-07225-z", "resourceTypeGeneral": "JournalArticle", "relatedIdentifierType": "DOI"}, {"relationType": "Cites", "relatedIdentifier": "10.1007/s13202-023-01710-6", "resourceTypeGeneral": "JournalArticle", "relatedIdentifierType": "DOI"}, {"relationType": "HasVersion", "relatedIdentifier": "10.5281/zenodo.24408075", "relatedIdentifierType": "DOI"}], "relatedItems": [], "sizes": [], "formats": [], "version": "1.0", "rightsList": [{"rights": "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International", "rightsUri": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode", "schemeUri": "https://spdx.org/licenses/", "rightsIdentifier": "cc-by-4.0", "rightsIdentifierScheme": "SPDX"}, {"rights": "Copyright (c) 2026 Min-Gi Kim. All rights reserved except as permitted under the stated license.", "rightsUri": "http://rightsstatements.org/vocab/InC/1.0/"}], "descriptions": [{"description": "Preprint \u2014 Not peer reviewed\n\n\u00a0\n\nThis exploratory study examines sensor confirmation timing and false-alarm duration in oil-well anomaly detection using Petrobras 3W Dataset 2.0.0.\n\n\u00a0\n\nThe study compares temporal sensor confirmation rules across 24 previously explored records containing 13 eligible anomaly events and 12,809 minutes of normal operation.\n\n\u00a0\n\nBoth v0.8 and v0.12 detected five events within five minutes, while normal-operation alarm duration decreased from 225 to 146 minutes. This comparison does not represent matched alarm budgets.\n\n\u00a0\n\nUnder separately matched supplementary alarm budgets, v0.11 and v0.12 each detected 5 of 13 events, while normal alarm duration decreased from 217 to 206 minutes (5.1%).\n\n\u00a0\n\nThe v0.7 baseline produced the shortest normal alarm duration (103 minutes) but detected only 4 of 13 events.\n\n\u00a0\n\nAn additional short-window rule (v0.19) detected one further type 7 event, yielding 6 of 13 detections and 184 normal alarm minutes.\n\n\u00a0\n\nAcross 15 previously unused intervals from previously studied wells, all evaluated OrganOS variants missed both eligible type 5 events.\n\n\u00a0\n\nA locally implemented, untuned Isolation Forest reference was also evaluated. This comparison does not reproduce a published benchmark protocol.\n\n\u00a0\n\nThese findings are exploratory. The comparison records were reused during candidate selection, and independent validation on previously unseen wells has not been completed.\n\n\u00a0\n\nThe accompanying reproduction package preserves experimental evidence, frozen parameters, code, and SHA-256 integrity information.\n\n\u00a0\n\nData source: Petrobras 3W Dataset 2.0.0.\n\n\u00a0\n\nReproducibility: The companion archive 3W_Preprint_Reproduction_Full_Package.zip is provided with the manuscript.", "descriptionType": "Abstract"}, {"lang": "eng", "description": "This manuscript is an exploratory technical preprint and has not undergone peer review.\n\n\u00a0\n\nThe reported results are based on previously examined Petrobras 3W records. The study does not establish superior performance on independent wells or in operational oil-field environments.\n\n\u00a0\n\nBoth positive and negative experimental outcomes are reported. Independent prospective validation remains necessary.", "descriptionType": "Other"}], "geoLocations": [], "fundingReferences": [], "xml": "", "url": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.24408074", "contentUrl": null, "metadataVersion": 0, "schemaVersion": "http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4", "source": "api", "isActive": true, "state": "findable", "reason": null, "viewCount": 0, "viewsOverTime": [], "downloadCount": 0, "downloadsOverTime": [], "referenceCount": 3, "citationCount": 0, "citationsOverTime": [], "partCount": 0, "partOfCount": 0, "versionCount": 1, "versionOfCount": 0, "created": "2026-11-20T23:11:50.000Z", "registered": "2026-11-20T23:11:50.000Z", "published": "2026", "updated": "2026-11-20T23:11:50.000Z"}, "relationships": {"client": {"data": {"id": "cern.zenodo", "type": "clients"}}, "provider": {"data": {"id": "cern", "type": "providers"}}, "media": {"data": {"id": "10.5281/zenodo.24408074", "type": "media"}}, "references": {"data": [{"id": "10.1007/s13202-023-01710-6", "type": "dois"}, {"id": "10.6084/m9.figshare.29205836.v1", "type": "dois"}, {"id": "10.1038/s41597-026-07225-z", "type": "dois"}]}, "citations": {"data": []}, "parts": {"data": []}, "partOf": {"data": []}, "versions": {"data": [{"id": "10.5281/zenodo.24408075", "type": "dois"}]}, "versionOf": {"data": []}}}}